qa-sentinels (1.4.7) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Guard tickets against probe-timing artifacts. Correlation now starts
    its death window after a five-minute settling period (QA_CORRELATE_SETTLE_S)
    and skips boots shorter than the remaining window
    (QA_CORRELATE_MIN_WINDOW_S), so startup and firmware-probe notices are
    not counted as pre-stop evidence.
  * Classify recovery/rescue exits and explicit reboot/poweroff targets as
    clean, record maintenance boots, and exclude them from unclean findings,
    repeat rates and correlation.
  * Treat per-init/per-resume notices (ATA DRM probe, Bluetooth firmware and
    Coded PHY, USB power-management, module taint) as non-ticketworthy.
    Probe-capability findings (hardware.coverage, hardware.vendor.missing)
    never become vendor tickets.
  * Require crash affinity to come from a recent process sample that names
    the same executable (QA_PROC_MATCH_WINDOW_S); stale PID samples and PID
    reuse now yield an unknown affinity instead of a fault-core verdict.
  * Count findings by distinct rows, not collection runs. pstore archives
    produce one finding per archived record with the panic timestamp and a
    kernel route for kernel panics.
  * Raise gate uses the real issue kind and severity, substantiates on a
    critical signal, and treats needs-root/coverage limitations as
    environmental.

